const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"How to Use Quotex Bot on Mobile with Lemur Browser 2026","datePublished":"2026-06-05","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"QuotexBot"}};
---
<Layout title="How to Use Quotex Bot on Mobile with Lemur Browser 2026" description="Complete guide to running the Quotex martingale trading bot on Android mobile using Lemur Browser Chrome extension support. Setup, tips and troubleshooting for mobile Quotex trading." keywords="quotex bot mobile, quotex bot android, lemur browser quotex, quotex mobile trading bot, qxbroker mobile bot, quotex chrome extension mobile, binary options bot android" schema={schema}>
  <Header/>
  <article class="blog-art">
    <div class="container blog-wrap">
      <header class="art-hdr">
        <div class="art-meta"><span class="badge badge-blue">Mobile Guide</span><span class="art-date">June 5, 2026 · 5 min read</span></div>
        <h1>How to Use Quotex Bot on Mobile with Lemur Browser</h1>
        <p class="art-lead">Quotex Bot works on Android mobile devices using Lemur Browser — a Chromium-based browser that supports Chrome extensions. This complete guide walks you through setup, configuration and tips for mobile trading.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="art-body">
        <h2>What is Lemur Browser?</h2>
        <p>Lemur Browser is an Android browser built on Chromium that supports Chrome extensions — something regular Chrome for Android does not support. This makes it the perfect solution for running Quotex Bot on mobile devices.</p>
        <div class="callout info"><strong>✅ Compatible:</strong> Android devices running Android 8.0 or higher. Lemur Browser is free to download from the Google Play Store.</div>
        <h2>Step 1: Install Lemur Browser</h2>
        <p>Open the Google Play Store on your Android device and search for <strong>Lemur Browser</strong>. Download and install it for free. Once installed, open Lemur Browser — it looks and feels similar to Chrome.</p>
        <h2>Step 2: Install Quotex Bot Extension in Lemur</h2>
        <p>In Lemur Browser, navigate to the Chrome Web Store by typing <code>chrome.google.com/webstore</code> in the address bar. Search for <strong>Quotex Bot</strong> and click <strong>Add to Chrome</strong>. The extension installs just like on desktop Chrome.</p>
        <p>After installation, tap the puzzle piece icon (🧩) in the Lemur toolbar to see your extensions. Pin Quotex Bot for easy access.</p>
        <h2>Step 3: Open Quotex Demo Trading Page</h2>
        <p>In Lemur Browser, go to <strong>qxbroker.com/en/demo-trade</strong>. The Quotex trading platform will load. Tap the Quotex Bot extension icon to open the bot sidebar on the right side of your screen.</p>
        <div class="callout warning"><strong>⚠️ Important:</strong> Keep the Trades panel at the bottom of the Quotex page visible at all times. The bot reads trade results from there — scrolling it away will cause the bot to malfunction.</div>
        <h2>Step 4: Configure and Start Trading</h2>
        <p>The mobile experience is identical to desktop. Select a preset (Conservative recommended for mobile), set your time interval, optionally configure Take Profit and Stop Loss, then tap <strong>Start Trading</strong>.</p>
        <ul class="art-list">
          <li>Use landscape mode for better visibility of the trading chart and sidebar</li>
          <li>Conservative preset is recommended on mobile — easier to monitor</li>
          <li>Set Stop Loss to protect against losing trades while you're mobile</li>
          <li>Enable Timer Stop to automatically end sessions after a set duration</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Mobile Trading Tips</h2>
        <ul class="art-list">
          <li><strong>Screen timeout:</strong> Set your phone to never sleep while trading — go to Settings → Display → Screen Timeout → Never</li>
          <li><strong>WiFi recommended:</strong> Use WiFi instead of mobile data for faster, more reliable trade execution</li>
          <li><strong>Battery:</strong> Keep your phone plugged in during trading sessions</li>
          <li><strong>Landscape mode:</strong> Rotate your phone for a better view of both the chart and bot sidebar</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Troubleshooting Common Mobile Issues</h2>
        <h3>Bot says "Could not find trading buttons"</h3>
        <p>This happens when the Quotex page hasn't fully loaded. Refresh the page and wait for all elements to appear before starting the bot.</p>
        <h3>Extension not appearing in Lemur</h3>
        <p>Go to Lemur settings → Extensions → ensure Quotex Bot is enabled. If not visible, reinstall from the Chrome Web Store.</p>
        <h3>Trades not being detected</h3>
        <p>Make sure the Trades panel is fully visible and not scrolled away. The bot needs to read results from the trade history list.</p>
        <div class="art-cta"><h3>Ready to Trade on Mobile?</h3><p>Install Quotex Bot and start automating on your Android device with Lemur Browser.</p><a href="https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/dbdhnfbjkakhilkkaoemgldcikboakdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4" fill="currentColor"/></svg> Add to Chrome — Free</a></div>
        <div class="art-nav"><a href="/blog/how-to-use-quotex-bot" class="btn btn-secondary">← Bot Tutorial</a><a href="/blog/best-trading-sequences" class="btn btn-secondary">Next: Best Sequences →</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Footer/><WhatsAppFloat/>
</Layout>
